{title: Sweet Hour of Prayer}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}
{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Sweet [C]hour of prayer, sweet [F]hour of prayer
That [C]calls me from a [G]world of care
And [C]bids me at my [F]Father's throne
Make [C]all my wants and [G]wishes [C]known
In [C]sea-sons [F]of dis[C]tress and grief
My [C]soul has [F]often [C]found re[G7]lief
And [C]oft escaped the [F]tempter's snare
By [C]thy return, sweet [G]hour of [C]prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Sweet [C]hour of prayer, sweet [F]hour of prayer
The [C]joys I feel, the [G]bliss I share
Of [C]those whose anxious [F]spirits burn
With [C]strong desires for [G]thy re[C]turn!
With [C]such I [F]hasten [C]to the place
Where [C]God my [F]Savior [C]shows his [G7]face
And [C]gladly take my [F]station there
And [C]wait for thee, sweet [G]hour of [C]prayer!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Sweet [C]hour of prayer, sweet [F]hour of prayer
Thy [C]wings shall my pe[G]tition bear
To [C]him whose truth and [F]faithfulness
En[C]gage the waiting [G7]soul to [C]bless
And [C]since he [F]bids me [C]seek his face
Be[C]lieve his [F]word, and [C]trust his [G7]grace
I'll [C]cast on [**]him my [F]every care
And [C]wait for thee, sweet [G]hour of [C]prayer.
{end_of_verse}
